  "metadata": {
    "source": "del Sagrado, del Aguila, and Orellana, Multi-objective ant colony optimization for requirements selection, Empirical Software Engineering 20 (2015) 577-610",
    "source_dataset": "Dataset 1, Tables 1 and 2",
    "adaptation_notes": [
      "The JSON preserves the 20 original candidate requirements before coupling and precedence preprocessing.",
      "Customer priorities are stored as multivalued satisfaction attributes ordered c1-c5.",
      "The paper defines global satisfaction as a weighted sum. NRP-Exp uses weighted_mean to preserve source ratings; multiply the aggregated value by 14, the sum of customer weights, to recover the paper scale.",
      "Paper implication ri => rj is represented as from=ri, to=rj, meaning that selecting ri requires rj.",
      "The paper evaluates effort bounds 25, 43, and 60, corresponding to 30%, 50%, and 70% of total effort."
    ],
